Well, I finally got the YODA patched version of 2.3 to run on my PC and
thought the light at the end of the debug tunnel was finally in sight,
but when I run the game, it goes for about 500 turns and ends
abruptly.  Nothing really seems obvious as to what causes this.  Once I
was simply walking through a door and pressed the 'L' key when the game
stopped and I had to cold boot.  Another time I had entered a shop and
picked up a couple of food rations which I sacrificed.  I got the
message "A four leaf clover appears at your feet," then, "% #&^TC
R)*G$*$V GU)X%FV#^ VUH...more," and then it died.  The last time I
played as a healer (all the other times were as a Jedi-knight) and when
the game ended I got a "divide error ... memory allocation error..."
before the game stopped and I was able to use ctrl-alt-del to reboot.
It doesn't look very promising. If anyone knows where the problems most
likely are, I'd appreciate the help.  In the meanwhile, I'm sending
2.3e to Rahul for posting.  It works OK as far as I can tell.

